# Loaded automatically by the Firebase CLI at deploy time and set in the
# function's runtime environment.
#
# NOT a secret -- this bucket name is public in firebase.json and in
# lib/services/storage_ref.dart. It lives here because index.js reads the
# bucket from the environment rather than hardcoding it, so that a
# misconfigured deploy fails loudly instead of silently sweeping the project's
# DEFAULT bucket, which is shared with an unrelated app.
#
# Bare bucket name, no gs:// prefix: this is passed to
# getStorage(app).bucket(...) in the Admin SDK. The Dart constant
# kLunaStorageBucket carries the gs:// form because the Flutter SDK wants a URL.
LUNA_STORAGE_BUCKET=teddy-2-20649-lunatrack-media
